ARCHITECTURE
  - SwiftUI View + @MainActor @Observable MediaPlayerPageModel (ADR-004). No business
    logic in the view body; all derivations (web useMemo `filtered`/`stats`/`volumeChartData`/
    `sourceData`) are model computed-properties.
  - The web TanStack queries are kept by name as the single KMP seam in
    MediaPlayerDataSource.swift (useMediaLatest → GET /media/latest, useMediaHistory → GET /media);
    only that file changes when the generated client lands (P1/S2-S3). The view never touches the network.
  - Charts are first-party Swift Charts (SectorMark / AreaMark+LineMark) — never a WKWebView.
  - Tokens (P2) for every color/typography (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSChartPalette);
    .regularMaterial for the web glass (ADR-005). Adaptive macOS (regular) + iOS (compact/regular)
    via horizontalSizeClass (charts row side-by-side vs stacked) (ADR-002/006).
  - SI boundary (P1/S5): the page carries no non-SI unit — audio_volume is an unitless Tesla
    loudness step (0…max) and elapsed/duration are milliseconds (time, already canonical). There is
    no miles/mph/psi/kWh quantity; values render directly via MediaPlayerFormat. Documented in the
    file header so the "never store/compute non-SI" rule is honored by construction.
  - Live freshness (ADR-013): MediaPlayerPageModel.isStale surfaces a >2-min staleness chip.
  - a11y (ADR-015): accessibilityLabel/Value/traits on every panel, chart, gauge, badge and the
    sortable headers; charts expose a single VoiceOver summary; Dynamic Type via tokens; light/dark/
    increased-contrast via the dynamic-color tokens; ≥44pt targets (Picker/Button defaults).
  - i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal via String(localized:"translation.<key>"); web key names kept.

